-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/5c59efe9-8f3e-5c49-aedf-2833d6cda207
-- title:
--   Lowering an occupied Hecke corner from level Mr to level M
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p \ne 2$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over the residue field factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, whose base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $M \ne 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$ with $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $\mathrm{Smin} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and consist, away from $p$, exactly of the primes at which $\bar\rho$ is ramified; it is assumed that every $q \in \mathrm{Smin}$ with $q \ne p$ divides $M$, that a prime $q \ne p$ dividing $M$ but not in $\mathrm{Smin}$ satisfies $q^2 \mid M$, that $q^2 \mid M$ implies $q^3 \nmid M$ for $q \ne p$, that $\bar\rho$ has unipotent characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on inertia at each $q \in \mathrm{Smin}$, $q \ne p$, and that $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ (a decomposition-stable free rank-one line on which inertia acts trivially modulo the line) whenever $p \mid M$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$, $r \nmid M$, $p \nmid r-1$, and such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $r$ a non-unit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ inducing the $r$-power map on the residue field of $P$, $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \ne (r+1)^2$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ have an integral structure, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(M)$ in weight $2$ generated away from $S$ to the residue field such that for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Put $L = Mr$. Suppose given a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $\mathbb{T}$, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^1(L) := \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_{\top}(L)^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal{O})$, an idempotent splitting $\mathrm{Sp}$ of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$ exhausting the maximal ideals and $e_j \in \mathfrak{m}_{j'} \iff j \ne j'$) and an index $i$ whose corner $e_i H^1(L)$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, together with maps $t$ and $c$ from the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid L$) and $\langle d \rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$) to $\mathbb{T}$ and to $\mathcal{O}$. Call a generator admissible if it is not $U_q$ for some $q \mid L$ with $q \nmid M$. The hypotheses are: every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts on $H^1(L)$ through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators `opFamily` of the admissible generators; $t(g)$ acts as `opFamily` $g$ for admissible $g$; $t(g) - c(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_i$ for admissible $g$; any $v \in H^1(L)$ such that for each admissible $g$ and each $k$ some power of $t(g)-c(g)$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k H^1(L)$ lies in the corner; the residue of $c(T_\ell)$ is $\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$; $c(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal for $q \mid M$, $q \ne p$, $q^2 \mid M$; $c(U_p)$ is a unit if $p \mid M$; $c(\langle d\rangle) \equiv 1$; the corner is non-zero; and the corner ring at $i$ acts faithfully on the corner. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $\mathbb{T}_0$ with a commutative ring structure, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure, a module structure on $H^1(M) := \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_{\top}(M)^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal{O})$ forming a scalar tower over $\mathcal{O}$ and module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, an idempotent splitting $\mathrm{Sp}_0$ with index $i_0$ whose corner in $H^1(M)$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, and maps $t_0, c_0$ on the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \notin S \cup \{r\}$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_q$ ($q \mid M$), $\langle d \rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$) with values in $\mathbb{T}_0$ and $\mathcal{O}$, such that: every element of $\mathbb{T}_0$ acts through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the whole range of `opFamily` at level $M$; $t_0(g)$ acts as `opFamily` $g$ for every generator $g$; $t_0(g) - c_0(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$ for every $g$; the corresponding cofullness criterion holds for all generators; the corner is non-zero; the corner ring at $i_0$ acts faithfully on it; $c(T_\ell) = c_0(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime with $\ell \notin S \cup \{r\}$ and $\ell \nmid L$; $c(U_q) = c_0(U_q)$ for $q$ prime dividing $M$; and $c_0(\langle d\rangle) - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   This is the level-lowering step at the auxiliary prime $r$: since $\bar\rho$ admits no level-raising congruence at $r$ (the condition $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2 \ne (r+1)^2$ together with $p \nmid r-1$), an occupied residual Hecke corner on the cohomology at level $Mr$ is transported to one at level $M$, with the same residual eigenvalues for the $T_\ell$, the $U_q$ with $q \mid M$, and trivial diamond residues, and now for the full family of operators away from $S \cup \{r\}$. It feeds the comparison of corners at the auxiliary level, in particular the freeness and rank computations for the ordinary $\Sigma$-corner and the identification of the corner Hecke ring at the auxiliary level.
